Every `{a,b}` group counts as glob syntax, and alternatives may contain `/`.
== args
docs/{v1}/{a,b}.md
{docs/x,docs/y}/*.md
== file docs/v1/a.md
---
description: A.
---
== file docs/v1/b.md
---
description: B.
---
== file docs/x/x.md
---
description: X.
---
== file docs/y/y.md
---
description: Y.
---
== stdout
glob view: docs/{v1}/{a,b}.md {docs/x,docs/y}/*.md
docs/v1/a.md (3 lines): description: "A."
docs/v1/b.md (3 lines): description: "B."
docs/x/x.md (3 lines): description: "X."
docs/y/y.md (3 lines): description: "Y."
== stderr
== exit 0
